IMPORT prelude
-- Running a rule that uses EVERY. The companion to every-example.l4, which
-- shows the shapes; this one shows the shapes working.
--
-- Every rule here names its group with `IN tenants` — the roll. That is what
-- makes it runnable: see "Where the group comes from" on EVERY.md. (An older
-- spelling put the same list in the WHO condition, as `WHO elem t tenants`.
-- That spelling is DEPRECATED as of 2026-09-08: it still runs and nothing
-- warns you, but `IN` is the one to write. every-example.l4 keeps one
-- labelled specimen of it so the shape stays recognisable.)

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF
    Landlord HAS name IS A STRING
    Tenant   HAS name IS A STRING

DECLARE Action IS ONE OF
    Sign    HAS signer IS AN Actor
    Deliver HAS who    IS AN Actor
    Pay     HAS payer  IS AN Actor, payee IS AN Actor, amount IS A NUMBER
    Receipt HAS issuer IS AN Actor, to    IS AN Actor, amount IS A NUMBER

theLandlord MEANS Landlord OF "Ms Ng"
alice       MEANS Tenant OF "Alice"
bob         MEANS Tenant OF "Bob"
carol       MEANS Tenant OF "Carol"
tenants     MEANS LIST alice, bob, carol

-- THE BARRIER. Every tenant signs; when the last of them has, the landlord
-- owes a delivery, and his five days run from that moment.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`the tenancy` MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t IN tenants
        MUST   Sign (EXACTLY t)
        WITHIN 14
        ONCE   ALL HAVE
        HENCE  (PARTY theLandlord MUST Deliver (EXACTLY theLandlord) WITHIN 5)
        LEST   BREACH

-- PROBES for the ground truth of etc/lts-reader-proxy/every-run-example.
-- Lines 1-38 are doc/reference/regulative/every-run-example.l4:1-38 verbatim
-- (the barrier rule and its declarations). Each #TRACE is the proxy position
-- (Alice signs at 1, Bob at 2, clock at 2) plus further events.

-- Q2/Q5: Carol signs at 9 -> the landlord's delivery is due 5 later (14).
#TRACE `the tenancy` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 1
  PARTY bob   DOES Sign bob   AT 2
  PARTY carol DOES Sign carol AT 9

-- Q2: Carol signs on the deadline day (14) -> delivery due by 19.
#TRACE `the tenancy` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 1
  PARTY bob   DOES Sign bob   AT 2
  PARTY carol DOES Sign carol AT 14

-- Q3: nothing by 14; the next event is at 15.
#TRACE `the tenancy` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 1
  PARTY bob   DOES Sign bob   AT 2
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 15

-- Q5: Carol signs at 9, the landlord delivers at 14 -> fulfilled.
#TRACE `the tenancy` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 1
  PARTY bob   DOES Sign bob   AT 2
  PARTY carol DOES Sign carol AT 9
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 14

-- Q5: ... and at 15 -> the landlord is in breach.
#TRACE `the tenancy` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 1
  PARTY bob   DOES Sign bob   AT 2
  PARTY carol DOES Sign carol AT 9
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 15

-- Q2: Alice signing again does not count for Carol.
#TRACE `the tenancy` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 1
  PARTY bob   DOES Sign bob   AT 2
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 3
